spec:
  grid: 16-25 rows x 16-25 cols, two colors (bg + fg)
  task: convert rough hand-drawn nested frame-and-blob diagram into clean canonical version
  objects:
    frame: closed simple curve of fg pixels (4-connected, each pixel has exactly 2 fg 4-neighbors), exactly 1 hole; wobble_ratio (size / ideal_perimeter) ~0.97-1.04; turns_per_pixel ~0.34-0.43; bbox 7x7 to 20x24
    blob: small filled fg cluster with no holes; size 4-11 pixels; bbox 2x2 to 4x4
  tree: containment hierarchy; frames contain children (frames or blobs) inside their hole
    nesting_depth: 1-2
    frames: 1-2 total
    blobs: 1-4 total
    total_objects: 2-6
    children_per_frame: 1-3
    outside_blobs: 0-1 (blobs not inside any frame, placed to one side of outermost frame)
  sibling_layout: siblings within a frame have distinct row-bands or col-bands (non-overlapping on at least one axis); their relative positions define canonical output layout
  output: canonical diagram; frame -> 1px rectangular border with 1-cell bg gap to children; blob -> single fg pixel; siblings separated by 1 bg cell; outside blobs get 3x3 bg slot adjacent to outermost frame
  bg_padding: drawing occupies most of the grid; remaining area is bg; min 0 padding on some sides [observed]

generation_strategy:
