  63:     """
  64:     Complete each lower foreground prefix by continuing the top complete column pattern in blue.
  65: 
  66:     Input structure
  67:     A black-background grid has one foreground color arranged in separated row-groups. The top row-group spans every column and is the complete reference pattern; each lower row-group starts at the left edge and contains a shorter prefix of the same column-state pattern.
  68: 
  69:     Rule
  70:     Keep all existing foreground pixels. For every lower row-group, compare its compressed sequence of nonempty row-offset states by column to the top pattern, then paint the missing suffix columns with blue using the remaining top states; if the lower group already reaches the top pattern's final state, continue that final state to the right edge.
  71: 
  72:     Key insight
